  "query_preview": "../Monday to Friday/...A series of disturbances will \nfollow behind the front on Sunday, keeping rain in the forecast\nMonday through early week. A low looks to swing up from the south\ninto the Haida Gwaii area late Monday through the day Tuesday, \nbringing some elevated winds into the southern panhandle alongside\nlight to moderate rain. This low looks to stay southward, not\npushing as far up into the panhandle as it clips the southern\ncoast, though some weak disturbances will continue to bring some\nrain to the northern panhandle / NE Gulf coast early through\nmidweek. Not expecting much overall for this quick moving low, \nwith 0.5 to 1.5 inches in 24 hrs expected for the southern \npanhandle, and around 0.6 inches or less for areas further \nnorthward impacted by the disturbances pushing across the Gulf. \n\nStill looking ahead to the next, larger system that is expected \nto develop in the western Gulf midweek. Uncertainty remains in the\nforecast with it being further ahead in time, looking to not \nimpact the panhandle until Thursday, with the setup / location of\nthe low center and its strength still being quite different \nacross guidance. Updates will be made as the system gets closer in\ntime and as confidence grows in the expected rain and wind \nimpacts. Generally expecting two solutions: a stronger low staying\nfurther west and not impacting the panhandle until later Thursday\nto Friday, and a low impacting the panhandle sooner Thursday but\nwith a bit weaker of a setup. Still overall looking to bring some\nelevated winds and rainfall to the area.",
